      "notes": "Schema is introspected from the engine's own signature plus every nested settings dataclass (21 root params, 26 sections, engine enum choices, effective defaults), so new parameters appear without a Rust change. Every terrain_demo.py flag is classified as a page field, a section field, a pinned param reported in `excluded` with a reason, or a non-params demo knob; unclassified flags fail the test. Validation runs the engine's constructors, so its error text is shown verbatim and the renderer only receives params it accepted. Known gap: colormap_srgb / output_srgb_eotf are TerrainRenderParams fields that the config factory does not accept (the demo assigns them after construction)."
